cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Alba: a full-duplex voice model on a 4 GB laptop GPU"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The alba-duplex-research authors"
date-released: 2026-11-05
version: "0.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Echolonius/alba-duplex-research"
abstract: >-
  Research code, frozen test definitions, results and a review paper from an attempt to fine-tune
  LFM3-Audio-2B into a single streaming full-duplex voice model that listens and talks in 80 ms steps on
  an RTX 3050 Laptop GPU with 4 GB of memory, including a failure analysis of the first two training runs.
keywords:
  - full-duplex spoken dialogue
  - turn-taking
  - speech language model
  - QLoRA
  - llama.cpp
  - CUDA graphs
